# ── Recognition models (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The app runs fully geometry-only with none of these set; recognition simply
# stays quiet. Supply URLs to enable camera-based part recognition.
#
# BEST PUBLIC STARTING POINT for industrial AR: Ultralytics YOLO (YOLO11 / v8)
# exported to ONNX — real-time, WebGPU-accelerated in ONNX Runtime Web, and the
# pipeline's decoder already speaks its output format (COCO-80 labels bundled).
#
# It detects generic objects (person, tools-ish), NOT your specific parts. For
# real part recognition, fine-tune on a few hundred labelled images of your
# parts and name the classes after your part IDs:
#     yolo train  model=yolo11n.pt data=parts.yaml imgsz=640
#     yolo export model=best.pt    format=onnx      opset=12
# then host best.onnx on your origin and point VITE_DETECTOR_MODEL_URL at it.
#
# Example (verify/self-host before production — do not rely on a third-party
# mirror staying up):
#   VITE_DETECTOR_MODEL_URL=https://your-host/models/yolo11n.onnx
VITE_DETECTOR_MODEL_URL=
VITE_CLASSIFIER_MODEL_URL=
VITE_SEGMENTER_MODEL_URL=

# Override the OpenCV.js bundle location if self-hosting instead of the CDN.
VITE_OPENCV_URL=
